1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,580
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,580 --> 00:00:05,230
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:05,230 --> 00:00:06,400
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,660 --> 00:00:09,490
I've worked drilling rigs
for thirty-one years.

5
00:00:09,650 --> 00:00:12,080
Two weeks on, one week
off,

6
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:14,980
twelve-hour hitches on a
steel rig floor.

7
00:00:15,230 --> 00:00:16,190
I had my right knee

8
00:00:16,190 --> 00:00:17,650
replaced two years ago.

9
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:19,920
It has hurt every day
since.

10
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:21,720
Not surgery pain.

11
00:00:21,760 --> 00:00:23,120
I know what that felt
like,

12
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:24,160
and it went away.

13
00:00:24,530 --> 00:00:25,510
This is different.

14
00:00:25,550 --> 00:00:26,090
Tight.

15
00:00:26,130 --> 00:00:26,860
Full.

16
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:27,810
Like a band around

17
00:00:27,810 --> 00:00:29,630
the joint that never
loosens.

18
00:00:29,840 --> 00:00:31,120
And for two years

19
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:32,550
I've been told the same
thing.

20
00:00:32,850 --> 00:00:33,690
Give it time.

21
00:00:33,850 --> 00:00:35,690
At six weeks it was
swelling,

22
00:00:35,690 --> 00:00:36,950
and swelling is normal.

23
00:00:37,190 --> 00:00:37,910
At three months,

24
00:00:37,910 --> 00:00:38,940
give it six.

25
00:00:38,980 --> 00:00:40,070
At six months,

26
00:00:40,070 --> 00:00:41,840
some knees take a full
year.

27
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:42,470
At a year,

28
00:00:42,470 --> 00:00:44,300
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

29
00:00:44,580 --> 00:00:45,920
And I didn't just wait.

30
00:00:46,080 --> 00:00:47,470
We went down the list.

31
00:00:47,990 --> 00:00:49,440
More physical therapy.

32
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:51,300
Every session on my week
off,

33
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:53,670
every exercise in the
bunkhouse on hitch.

34
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:54,850
I got stronger.

35
00:00:54,900 --> 00:00:56,490
The tightness never moved.

36
00:00:56,530 --> 00:00:57,960
The pain pills helped,

37
00:00:57,960 --> 00:00:59,170
and that was the problem.

38
00:00:59,530 --> 00:01:01,460
I'm already on enough
every morning,

39
00:01:01,460 --> 00:01:02,400
and nobody could tell me

40
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:03,450
when I'd get to stop.

41
00:01:03,890 --> 00:01:05,430
Then a nerve block.

42
00:01:05,520 --> 00:01:07,280
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

43
00:01:07,390 --> 00:01:08,740
And after that, a second

44
00:01:08,740 --> 00:01:09,840
operation to go back

45
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:10,990
in and do it over.

46
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:12,000
I said no.

47
00:01:12,220 --> 00:01:13,730
Every morning on hitch

48
00:01:13,730 --> 00:01:15,240
I stepped off my bunk

49
00:01:15,240 --> 00:01:16,250
and my knee felt like

50
00:01:16,250 --> 00:01:18,010
a band was wrapped around
it,

51
00:01:18,010 --> 00:01:20,250
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

52
00:01:20,690 --> 00:01:22,120
Every morning I took
something

53
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:23,630
for it, pulled on my
coveralls

54
00:01:23,630 --> 00:01:24,580
and went to work.

55
00:01:24,790 --> 00:01:25,900
Couldn't take the stairs
up

56
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:27,070
to the rig floor

57
00:01:27,070 --> 00:01:29,050
without stopping halfway,

58
00:01:29,050 --> 00:01:31,350
couldn't stand through a
twelve-hour tower without

59
00:01:31,350 --> 00:01:33,360
hunting for something to
lean on,

60
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:34,860
couldn't sit through my
grandson's

61
00:01:34,860 --> 00:01:36,270
game on my week off

62
00:01:36,270 --> 00:01:38,440
without shifting every two
minutes.

63
00:01:38,700 --> 00:01:39,970
It woke me at night,

64
00:01:39,970 --> 00:01:41,950
and it turned ordinary
things,

65
00:01:41,950 --> 00:01:44,030
like climbing into the
truck or getting

66
00:01:44,030 --> 00:01:45,950
down to look under the
pipe rack,

67
00:01:45,950 --> 00:01:47,080
into a decision.

68
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:48,820
I started doing the math
on how

69
00:01:48,820 --> 00:01:50,570
many hitches I had left in
me.

70
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:51,930
After a long and serious

71
00:01:51,930 --> 00:01:52,810
talk with my wife,

72
00:01:52,810 --> 00:01:54,500
I went back in one more
time.

73
00:01:54,850 --> 00:01:56,030
That was the fourth set

74
00:01:56,030 --> 00:01:57,570
of X-rays on this knee.

75
00:01:57,860 --> 00:01:59,460
And like the three before
it,

76
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:02,080
the answer was everything
looks great.

77
00:02:02,190 --> 00:02:04,540
No loosening, no
infection,

78
00:02:04,540 --> 00:02:05,560
nothing wrong.

79
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:06,630
Only this time there

80
00:02:06,630 --> 00:02:07,870
was no new number.

81
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:10,230
Nobody said give it
another six months.

82
00:02:10,290 --> 00:02:11,870
There was nothing left to
give it.

83
00:02:11,910 --> 00:02:12,770
I sat in the parking

84
00:02:12,770 --> 00:02:13,750
lot for a while.

85
00:02:13,790 --> 00:02:14,780
Okay, I thought.

86
00:02:14,820 --> 00:02:16,110
Then explain this.

87
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:18,470
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

88
00:02:18,470 --> 00:02:19,920
I hit my breaking point.

89
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:22,250
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

90
00:02:22,440 --> 00:02:24,980
Everyone in the bunkhouse
was asleep

91
00:02:24,980 --> 00:02:26,290
and I was sitting on the
edge

92
00:02:26,290 --> 00:02:27,550
of my bunk with my leg

93
00:02:27,550 --> 00:02:28,930
up on a cooler,

94
00:02:28,930 --> 00:02:30,550
trying to find any angle

95
00:02:30,550 --> 00:02:32,090
where it didn't feel like
something

96
00:02:32,090 --> 00:02:33,920
was wrapped around my knee

97
00:02:33,920 --> 00:02:34,830
and tightening.

98
00:02:35,140 --> 00:02:37,440
My wife was four hundred
miles away.

99
00:02:37,580 --> 00:02:38,430
By then

100
00:02:38,430 --> 00:02:40,130
I'd stopped telling her on
the phone.

101
00:02:40,460 --> 00:02:41,670
And I just thought,

102
00:02:41,670 --> 00:02:43,320
is this really my life
now?

103
00:02:43,360 --> 00:02:44,730
I can't live like this.

104
00:02:44,770 --> 00:02:46,790
So I made myself a
promise.

105
00:02:46,910 --> 00:02:48,050
I wouldn't go a day

106
00:02:48,050 --> 00:02:49,660
without looking for an
answer.

107
00:02:49,770 --> 00:02:51,160
And when I found one,

108
00:02:51,160 --> 00:02:52,320
I'd share it with everyone

109
00:02:52,320 --> 00:02:53,660
going through the same
thing.

110
00:02:53,960 --> 00:02:54,860
So I got my phone

111
00:02:54,860 --> 00:02:56,120
out and went looking.

112
00:02:56,240 --> 00:02:57,490
Not for a product.

113
00:02:57,660 --> 00:02:59,050
For an explanation.

114
00:02:59,350 --> 00:03:00,930
Mayo Clinic forums,

115
00:03:00,930 --> 00:03:03,160
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

116
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:04,530
doctor videos,

117
00:03:04,530 --> 00:03:05,990
medical animations.

118
00:03:06,630 --> 00:03:08,670
And that's when I found a
video

119
00:03:08,670 --> 00:03:10,550
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

120
00:03:10,590 --> 00:03:12,830
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

121
00:03:12,830 --> 00:03:14,850
had been through exactly
this.

122
00:03:15,060 --> 00:03:17,670
But before I say anything
else,

123
00:03:17,670 --> 00:03:19,120
I want to be straight with
you.

124
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:21,410
You've already had
something work fast.

125
00:03:21,450 --> 00:03:22,270
The ice.

126
00:03:22,310 --> 00:03:24,010
The first week of a new
pill.

127
00:03:24,100 --> 00:03:25,830
The good day after a
session.

128
00:03:26,020 --> 00:03:27,340
Then it wore off.

129
00:03:27,390 --> 00:03:29,510
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

130
00:03:29,870 --> 00:03:31,850
Fast relief isn't relief.

131
00:03:32,030 --> 00:03:32,950
It's a preview.

132
00:03:33,260 --> 00:03:34,370
So I'm not going to tell

133
00:03:34,370 --> 00:03:35,440
you this works fast.

134
00:03:35,480 --> 00:03:36,320
It doesn't.

135
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:38,300
But if you're willing to
be patient,

136
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:39,160
and to look at what's

137
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:40,710
going on around your new
knee

138
00:03:40,710 --> 00:03:42,250
instead of inside it,
there

139
00:03:42,250 --> 00:03:44,320
is a real reason it still
hurts.

140
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:46,300
And something you can do
about it.

141
00:03:46,620 --> 00:03:48,720
Let me explain what he
said,

142
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:50,090
because this is what
changed

143
00:03:50,090 --> 00:03:51,180
everything for me.

144
00:03:51,220 --> 00:03:52,890
He started with the
basics.

145
00:03:53,110 --> 00:03:54,580
A knee replacement takes
out

146
00:03:54,580 --> 00:03:56,200
the worn joint surfaces

147
00:03:56,200 --> 00:03:58,100
and puts in metal and
plastic.

148
00:03:58,230 --> 00:03:59,930
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

149
00:03:59,930 --> 00:04:01,550
you had before the
operation.

150
00:04:01,820 --> 00:04:03,360
That part I already knew.

151
00:04:03,810 --> 00:04:05,160
But then he explained
something

152
00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:06,580
nobody had ever told me.

153
00:04:06,740 --> 00:04:07,480
He said,

154
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:08,860
think about a swollen foot

155
00:04:08,860 --> 00:04:10,190
inside a work boot.

156
00:04:10,370 --> 00:04:11,940
The boot didn't shrink.

157
00:04:12,130 --> 00:04:14,000
Your foot is taking up
more room,

158
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:15,460
so everything feels
cramped

159
00:04:15,460 --> 00:04:16,920
and tight and squeezed.

160
00:04:17,310 --> 00:04:18,560
Your new knee sits

161
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:19,790
in a limited space

162
00:04:19,790 --> 00:04:22,130
with living tissue packed
all around it.

163
00:04:22,460 --> 00:04:24,270
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

164
00:04:24,270 --> 00:04:25,860
had to work through that
tissue.

165
00:04:26,130 --> 00:04:28,360
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

166
00:04:28,660 --> 00:04:30,010
At first that's normal.

167
00:04:30,350 --> 00:04:31,860
But in some people that
swelling can

168
00:04:31,860 --> 00:04:34,330
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

169
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:35,840
And swollen tissue takes
up more

170
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:37,450
room than calm tissue
does.

171
00:04:37,570 --> 00:04:38,900
So when you bend,

172
00:04:38,900 --> 00:04:40,520
that tissue gets
compressed.

173
00:04:40,580 --> 00:04:41,800
When you straighten,

174
00:04:41,800 --> 00:04:43,170
it gets pulled tight.

175
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:44,400
That's the band.

176
00:04:44,470 --> 00:04:46,690
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

177
00:04:46,770 --> 00:04:47,560
And you start being

178
00:04:47,560 --> 00:04:48,760
the one who says,

179
00:04:48,760 --> 00:04:50,120
you boys go ahead.

180
00:04:50,160 --> 00:04:51,190
I'll stay here.

181
00:04:51,420 --> 00:04:53,150
And that's exactly why

182
00:04:53,150 --> 00:04:54,950
so much of what I'd tried

183
00:04:54,950 --> 00:04:56,040
hadn't worked.

184
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:57,670
Physical therapy

185
00:04:57,670 --> 00:05:00,010
strengthens the muscles
around the knee.

186
00:05:00,050 --> 00:05:00,950
Worth doing,

187
00:05:00,950 --> 00:05:01,930
and I'd done it.

188
00:05:02,230 --> 00:05:03,730
It does nothing about
tissue

189
00:05:03,730 --> 00:05:04,860
taking up room.

190
00:05:05,010 --> 00:05:06,380
A nerve block quiets

191
00:05:06,380 --> 00:05:07,930
the nerve carrying the
signal.

192
00:05:08,310 --> 00:05:10,680
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

193
00:05:10,970 --> 00:05:12,630
But when that irritated
tissue

194
00:05:12,630 --> 00:05:14,120
finally calms down,

195
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:15,710
it holds less fluid,

196
00:05:15,710 --> 00:05:17,250
and it takes up less room.

197
00:05:17,570 --> 00:05:19,040
Less room taken up

198
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:21,260
means less pressure
squeezing the joint.

199
00:05:21,520 --> 00:05:23,230
That's what takes the
pressure off.

200
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:24,990
After two years of this,

201
00:05:24,990 --> 00:05:26,560
it finally made sense.

202
00:05:26,880 --> 00:05:28,850
The problem was never the
new knee.

203
00:05:29,060 --> 00:05:30,870
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

204
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:32,640
He calls it the squeeze.

205
00:05:32,680 --> 00:05:34,990
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

206
00:05:35,200 --> 00:05:36,470
I'd bought knee pads,

207
00:05:36,470 --> 00:05:39,360
compression braces to wear
under my coveralls,

208
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:41,910
creams, half of Amazon
really,

209
00:05:41,910 --> 00:05:43,140
and all any of it gave

210
00:05:43,140 --> 00:05:44,260
me was an hour.

211
00:05:44,620 --> 00:05:45,620
I even looked at going

212
00:05:45,620 --> 00:05:46,870
to a clinic for the light

213
00:05:46,870 --> 00:05:48,680
therapy on my week off.

214
00:05:48,840 --> 00:05:50,540
But at $200 a session

215
00:05:50,540 --> 00:05:52,350
with nothing covered by
insurance,

216
00:05:52,350 --> 00:05:53,990
that was a quick no.

217
00:05:54,030 --> 00:05:55,520
Then one night I went back

218
00:05:55,520 --> 00:05:57,080
to that knee replacement
group

219
00:05:57,080 --> 00:05:58,270
and actually read it.

220
00:05:58,480 --> 00:05:59,750
Thousands of people,

221
00:05:59,750 --> 00:06:01,360
years out from surgery,

222
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:04,690
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

223
00:06:04,690 --> 00:06:05,960
nobody could explain.

224
00:06:06,220 --> 00:06:07,980
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

225
00:06:07,980 --> 00:06:09,940
the same thing kept coming
up.

226
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:11,560
This one device,

227
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:13,040
and people saying it was
the first

228
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:14,330
thing that made a
difference.

229
00:06:14,590 --> 00:06:16,150
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

230
00:06:16,150 --> 00:06:17,070
alright, here it comes,

231
00:06:17,070 --> 00:06:18,520
he's selling me something,

232
00:06:18,520 --> 00:06:20,530
let me shut that down
right now.

233
00:06:20,580 --> 00:06:22,270
I'm only here because I
made myself

234
00:06:22,270 --> 00:06:24,330
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

235
00:06:24,330 --> 00:06:25,330
that if I ever found

236
00:06:25,330 --> 00:06:26,440
something that helped,

237
00:06:26,440 --> 00:06:27,490
I'd say so.

238
00:06:27,620 --> 00:06:29,440
It's called the KenRelief

239
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:31,000
Red Light Therapy Wrap.

240
00:06:31,040 --> 00:06:32,150
At first glance

241
00:06:32,150 --> 00:06:33,100
I didn't buy it.

242
00:06:33,300 --> 00:06:34,500
It looked like the cheap

243
00:06:34,500 --> 00:06:36,330
knee sleeves off Amazon

244
00:06:36,330 --> 00:06:37,750
that did nothing for me.

245
00:06:37,990 --> 00:06:39,680
But I went to their
website anyway,

246
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:40,540
just to see what all

247
00:06:40,540 --> 00:06:41,740
the fuss was about.

248
00:06:41,980 --> 00:06:44,320
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

249
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:47,190
charge $200 a session for,

250
00:06:47,190 --> 00:06:50,280
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

251
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:51,400
in a wrap you plug

252
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:52,690
into the wall at home.

253
00:06:52,950 --> 00:06:54,650
Two hundred and forty
lights.

254
00:06:54,760 --> 00:06:57,180
Red at 660 nanometers

255
00:06:57,180 --> 00:06:59,470
and near-infrared at 850,

256
00:06:59,470 --> 00:07:01,550
run together for the
strongest effect.

257
00:07:01,680 --> 00:07:03,090
Four strength levels.

258
00:07:03,210 --> 00:07:05,030
A five to thirty minute
timer.

259
00:07:05,260 --> 00:07:07,400
Then I saw the guarantee.

260
00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:08,880
Ninety days.

261
00:07:09,030 --> 00:07:10,780
Results or your money
back,

262
00:07:10,780 --> 00:07:13,150
no questions, no store
credit,

263
00:07:13,150 --> 00:07:15,440
and you don't even send it
back.

264
00:07:15,820 --> 00:07:18,440
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

265
00:07:18,440 --> 00:07:20,310
days to change my mind.

266
00:07:20,410 --> 00:07:21,860
There wasn't much to lose,

267
00:07:21,860 --> 00:07:23,070
so I ordered it.

268
00:07:23,310 --> 00:07:24,670
Two of them, actually.

269
00:07:24,880 --> 00:07:26,810
Only the right knee was
replaced,

270
00:07:26,810 --> 00:07:29,350
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

271
00:07:29,350 --> 00:07:30,510
and I'd done it on a steel

272
00:07:30,510 --> 00:07:31,900
floor for two years.

273
00:07:31,940 --> 00:07:34,010
The left one was carrying
the difference.

274
00:07:34,240 --> 00:07:36,070
It came on my week off,

275
00:07:36,070 --> 00:07:38,460
and I strapped it on
expecting nothing,

276
00:07:38,460 --> 00:07:39,670
because I'd been let down

277
00:07:39,670 --> 00:07:41,600
too many times to get
excited.

278
00:07:41,930 --> 00:07:43,670
What I felt was warmth.

279
00:07:43,710 --> 00:07:45,490
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

280
00:07:45,820 --> 00:07:46,770
More like it was coming

281
00:07:46,770 --> 00:07:48,370
from inside the knee

282
00:07:48,370 --> 00:07:49,910
